<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5946" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιμέλας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μέλαινα,
			-μέλᾰν,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>black all round:</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always epith. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρένες</span>
			(best written divisim, as by <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i> critics), <i>darkened on either side,</i> of strong
			emotions, as anger, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				17.83
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.661
			</span></i>; courage, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.499
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				573
			</span></i>: prob. metaph. from an angry sea. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κόνις</span>
			<i>coal-black</i> dust, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.738
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Theodorid.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
